1. THE THREE GATES ON THE DOMAIN |p|_1 <= m (exact integers; the difference in the n-th self-creation's tick, root-free minus whole-root)
   m = 16: 136 values of p . p on |p|_1 <= m, n = 1 .. 17: gate (A) later than the whole root by at most 3 (at p . p = 89, n = [14]), identical for 1 of 136 values of W; gate (B) later by at most 1 (at p . p = 12, n = [16]), identical for 38 of 136; neither gate is ever earlier
   m = 64: 2359 values of p . p on |p|_1 <= m, n = 1 .. 65: gate (A) later than the whole root by at most 3 (at p . p = 557, n = [59]), identical for 1 of 2359 values of W; gate (B) later by at most 1 (at p . p = 44, n = [64]), identical for 231 of 2359; neither gate is ever earlier
   m = 100: 6017 values of p . p on |p|_1 <= m, n = 1 .. 101: gate (A) later than the whole root by at most 3 (at p . p = 998, n = [93]), identical for 1 of 6017 values of W; gate (B) later by at most 1 (at p . p = 68, n = [100]), identical for 444 of 6017; neither gate is ever earlier
   m = 128: 10094 values of p . p on |p|_1 <= m, n = 1 .. 128: gate (A) later than the whole root by at most 3 (at p . p = 1259, n = [119]), identical for 1 of 10094 values of W; gate (B) later by at most 1 (at p . p = 88, n = [126, 127, 128]), identical for 576 of 10094; neither gate is ever earlier
   the bound: (B) differs from the whole root by at most ceil((n - 1) / m), i.e. by at most 1 for n <= m + 1;
   (A) differs by ceil(n gamma) - 1 - floor((n - 1) E' / m): 0 at p = 0, exactly 1 at gamma = 2, at most 3 on the domain (gamma <= 2), as enumerated above

2. THE MUON OF SERIES S (m = Q S M = 64 x 1 x 207 = 13248; c^2 = [1, 3]); the 64th self-creation and the beta click
   p = 0: W = 175509504, E' = 13248, W - E'^2 = 0 (a perfect square: True); the 64th self-creation: whole root 64 (the register's pin), gate (A) 64, gate (B) 64; the beta click = decay + the product's flight (328 intervals as run): whole root 392 (run 392), (A) about 392 to 392, (B) 392; the largest difference over n = 1 .. 64: (A) 0, (B) 0
   p = 3640: W = 215258304, E' = 14671, W - E'^2 = 20063 (a perfect square: False); the 64th self-creation: whole root 70 (the register's pin), gate (A) 71, gate (B) 70; the beta click = decay + the product's flight (299 intervals as run): whole root 369 (run 369), (A) about 370 to 369, (B) 369; the largest difference over n = 1 .. 64: (A) 2, (B) 0
   p = 12856: W = 671339712, E' = 25910, W - E'^2 = 11612 (a perfect square: False); the 64th self-creation: whole root 124 (the register's pin), gate (A) 126, gate (B) 124; the beta click = decay + the product's flight (221 intervals as run): whole root 345 (run 345), (A) about 347 to 346, (B) 345; the largest difference over n = 1 .. 64: (A) 2, (B) 0

3. THE COUNTERS' BOUND (the working bound 2^63 - 1 on t^2 m^2 and n^2 W)
   m = 13248: t^2 m^2 <= 2^63 - 1 up to t = 229242 intervals; n^2 W <= 2^63 - 1 up to n = 114621 self-creations at gamma = 2 (W = 4 m^2)
   m = 64: t^2 m^2 <= 2^63 - 1 up to t = 47453132 intervals; n^2 W <= 2^63 - 1 up to n = 23726566 self-creations at gamma = 2 (W = 4 m^2)
   m = 1048576: t^2 m^2 <= 2^63 - 1 up to t = 2896 intervals; n^2 W <= 2^63 - 1 up to n = 1448 self-creations at gamma = 2 (W = 4 m^2)
   m = 16777216: t^2 m^2 <= 2^63 - 1 up to t = 181 intervals; n^2 W <= 2^63 - 1 up to n = 90 self-creations at gamma = 2 (W = 4 m^2)
   the registered covariant worlds run 420 ticks (j4_muon_3640.json): the muon's products stay below 2^49 without any reset

4. THE RESET: the whole-root gate is periodic in n with period m and shift E' (T_(n + m) = T_n + E'), a check on the muon:
   p = 3640: T_(n + m) - T_n = E' = 14671 for every n <= m + 1: True; the shift is the elapsed ticks, read without a root
   p = 12856: T_(n + m) - T_n = E' = 25910 for every n <= m + 1: True; the shift is the elapsed ticks, read without a root
   gate (B) has no exact period (its shift per m self-creations is sqrt(W), not an integer); a reset of (t, n) to (0, 0) without a carried remainder
   changes the ticks: the next self-creation would fall at floor(gamma) + 1 = 2 intervals for every 1 < gamma < 2 (a rate 1/2 in place of 1/gamma)
